## Examples (Ví dụ)

### Ví dụ 1: React Component Testing

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: React component test
describe('UserProfile', () => {
  it('displays user name and avatar', () => {
    const user = { name: 'John Doe', avatar: '/john.jpg' };
    render(<UserProfile user={user} />);
    
    expect(screen.getByText('John Doe')).toBeInTheDocument();
    expect(screen.getByAltText('John Doe')).toHaveAttribute('src', '/john.jpg');
  });
  
  it('shows loading state', () => {
    render(<UserProfile loading={true} />);
    expect(screen.getByRole('progressbar')).toBeInTheDocument();
  });
  
  it('shows error state', () => {
    render(<UserProfile error="Failed to load" />);
    expect(screen.getByText('Failed to load')).toBeInTheDocument();
  });
});
```

### Ví dụ 2: API Integration Test

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: API integration test
describe('Orders API', () => {
  let authToken: string;
  
  beforeAll(async () => {
    const login = await request(app)
      .post('/api/auth/login')
      .send({ email: 'test@example.com', password: 'password' });
    authToken = login.body.token;
  });
  
  describe('POST /api/orders', () => {
    it('creates order with valid data', async () => {
      const res = await request(app)
        .post('/api/orders')
        .set('Authorization', `Bearer ${authToken}`)
        .send({
          items: [{ productId: 'prod_123', quantity: 2 }],
          shippingAddress: { street: '123 Main St' }
        });
      
      expect(res.status).toBe(201);
      expect(res.body).toMatchObject({
        id: expect.any(String),
        status: 'pending',
        total: expect.any(Number)
      });
    });
    
    it('returns 400 for invalid data', async () => {
      const res = await request(app)
        .post('/api/orders')
        .set('Authorization', `Bearer ${authToken}`)
        .send({ items: [] }); // Empty items
      
      expect(res.status).toBe(400);
      expect(res.body.errors).toContainEqual(
        expect.objectContaining({ field: 'items' })
      );
    });
  });
});
```

## Anti Patterns (Các pattern cần tránh)

### 1. No Mocks - Brittle Tests
```typescript
// ❌ BAD: Testing with real external service
it('gets user data', async () => {
  const user = await RealExternalService.getUser('123'); // Real call!
});

// ✅ GOOD: Mock external dependencies
it('gets user data', async () => {
  mockExternalService.getUser.mockResolvedValue({ id: '123', name: 'John' });
  const user = await userService.getUser('123');
  expect(user.name).toBe('John');
});
```

### 2. Testing Implementation Details
```typescript
// ❌ BAD: Testing private methods
it('sorts items correctly', () => {
  const service = new ItemService();
  const sorted = service.privateSortMethod(items); // Bad!
});

// ✅ GOOD: Test observable behavior
it('items sorted by date', () => {
  const service = new ItemService();
  const result = service.getItems({ sortBy: 'date' });
  expect(result[0].date).toBeBefore(result[1].date);
});
```

### 3. Flaky E2E Tests
```typescript
// ❌ BAD: No wait strategy
it('user logs in', () => {
  cy.visit('/login');
  cy.get('#username').type('user');
  cy.get('#password').type('pass');
  cy.get('button[type="submit"]').click();
  cy.contains('Welcome'); // Flaky!
});

// ✅ GOOD: Explicit waits
it('user logs in', () => {
  cy.visit('/login');
  cy.get('#username').type('user');
  cy.get('#password').type('pass');
  cy.get('button[type="submit"]').click();
  cy.get('[data-testid="welcome-message"]')
    .should('be.visible')
    .and('contain.text', 'Welcome');
});
```

## Best Practices (Thực hành tốt nhất)

1. **Follow test pyramid**: More unit, less E2E
2. **Test behavior, not implementation**: Focus on outcomes
3. **Keep tests independent**: No shared state
4. **Use meaningful names**: Test purpose clear
5. **Follow FIRST principles**: Fast, Independent, Repeatable, Self-validating, Timely
6. **Mock external dependencies**: Tests should be reliable
7. **Arrange-Act-Assert**: Clear test structure
8. **One assertion focus**: Multiple small tests vs one big test
9. **Maintain test code**: As important as production code
10. **Review test coverage**: Regular analysis

